9. Hypotheses and Kill Criteria

All thresholds are placeholders. A failed hypothesis demotes the component; it is not reinterpreted.

Hypothesis Operational statement Decision rule
H1 Energy In \Omega, a bioenergy configuration achieves \phi_B\geq0.20 over \geq30 consecutive days, worst 7-day \phi_B\geq0.05, exceeds the plant-free soil-MFC control by the relative gate \Delta P_{\mathrm{plant}}\geq0.10\,P_{\mathrm{PMFC}}, and meets the absolute gate \Delta P_{\mathrm{plant}}\geq20\ \mu\mathrm{W} as a 30-day mean and \geq10\ \mu\mathrm{W} above the soil-MFC control. Fail: bioenergy becomes sidecar signal or trickle source.
H2 Cooperation At equal sensing, compute, and airtime budgets, cooperation lowers held-out \mathrm{RMSE}_\theta by \geq10\% or false alarms by \geq20\%, relative to the centralised weighted least-squares comparator, within the energy multiplier of 2. Fail: Track A reverts to isolated nodes plus gateway aggregation.
H3 Water Versus the pre-registered strongest baseline (Arm 3), ARBOR reduces litres per tree by \geq10\% with tree health non-inferior over one full growing season. Fail: report savings relative to timer only.
H4 Reservoir \Delta_{43}\geq0.05 on held-out plants with lower 95\% bootstrap bound \geq0, and failure of the pre-specified dead-plant and plant-swap controls. Fail: plant signals are not used for decisions.
H5 Resilience During a 72 h gateway outage, \geq95\% of nodes keep soil moisture, node health, and a daily summary, and resume consensus within one event-triggered cycle after restoration. Fail: redesign local buffering.
H6 Integration Integrated node improves at least one pre-specified outcome over Track A at cost and maintenance \leq(1+\kappa)\times Track A. Fail: conclude Track A is the architecture.
