C Plant-reservoir estimation science Solar (same as Track A) Sentinel-plant leaf thickness or electrophysiology plus Track A sensors Recommendation only Must pass the Appendix H gate

C.2 Node roles (normative)

A sensing node measures, locally filters, stores, and transmits on an event or periodic schedule. It has no irrigation actuation. An actuation node or valve controller receives authenticated irrigation commands, enforces the local safety envelope, and logs metered volume; it must refuse any command that violates the envelope, even if the command originates from the gateway. A cluster head or gateway aggregates, forwards to the cloud, and distributes model updates; it is not required for local safety or for basic threshold irrigation. A sentinel plant node is Track C only: higher sensor density, higher maintenance, no actuation authority.

C.3 Failure modes and required behaviour

Failure Required behaviour
Gateway outage Nodes continue threshold irrigation from local rules; store readings; backfill when the gateway returns
Sensor drift or calibration expiry Node flagged degraded; readings excluded from irrigation decisions; alert raised
Battery low Node enters low-power mode: hourly heartbeat only; no actuation; no reservoir inference
Valve command fails or meter shows no flow Retry once, then alert; log as irrigation failure, not as water saved
Rain forecast error Safety envelope caps volume; soil-moisture upper bound prevents waterlogging
Neighbour node failure Gossip averaging reweights; no single neighbour may contribute more than 50% of a node’s estimate

