Appendix L — Quick-Reference Cards (For Field Teams)

L.1 Field-installation card

Check soil texture and record it; do not guess. Take a gravimetric sample adjacent to the sensor, at the same depth and the same hour. Install the sensor at the pre-registered depth; record depth, orientation, and calibration ID. Log soil temperature with the first reading. Check battery or panel voltage and record it. Test one uplink and confirm gateway receipt. Photograph the installation; record GPS where permitted and the node ID. Set the node’s calibration-expiry date in the log; do not leave it blank.

L.2 Irrigation-safety card

Never irrigate above 90% of field capacity. Never exceed the maximum single-event volume on the node’s label. If the sensor is flagged degraded, do not irrigate from that sensor. If rain is at least 5 mm in the past 24 h, skip. If in doubt, do not irrigate. Log the doubt.

L.3 Data-quality card

A reading without calibration metadata is not a measurement. A model estimate is not a direct measurement. A biological signal is not a diagnosis. When in doubt, flag the reading degraded and let a human decide.

